I find the final run is almost all tool based. The Ascension Kit is
critical. Let's take it Plane by Plane:

In General
----------
You need all of your resistances, magic cancellation, magic resistance,
and reflection. Also stock up on !oFH and food for the riders. Finally
make sure that you have instakill (wand or finger of death, or my
favorite: a cockatrice corpse) and a way to confused (booze) and
unconfused (blessed unihorn). In general I find that conflict is
useful on the planes as it destracts the enemies.

Earth
-----
Rodney will show. Get rid of him quick.

You need digging. I hope you saved all of those wands of digging.

Read a gold detect scroll while confused. It'll point you to portal.

Air
---
Levitation is the key to this plane. 

Go ahead and conflict.

Air elementals are very annoying. With the HP you have however you can
just bash them to death. If you like you can teleport them away from
you.

You should start seeing Archons. They are nasty. The double whammy of
blinding you and gating in more monsters can be overwhelming. I use
a multi pronged attack against them:

1) Eyes of the Overworld. Compeltely elminates the blinding problem.
2) conflict. Keeps the hordes occupied.
3) Speed to outrun the competition.
4) instakill. Cockatrice corpses are very useful here.

Fire
----
Use confused gold detect to get all the traps. You'll have to search out
the magic portal from the fire traps though.

More Archons. Same deal as above.

Stay conflicted

You're not really in any hurry here. Just take your time and find the portal.

Water
-----
Genocide all ';' and you can pretty much relax.

The portal moves so you'll just have to wait until it uncovers.

May want to remove conflict here. I forgot this weekend so I didn't get
my Angel on the Astral.

Go ahead and rest up, heal up, charge up (confused charging), and prep
for the final battle.

Astral
------
Actually I found conflict useful. And I got a cockatrice corpse upon
entering. It clears out most of the riff-raff.

Use range weapons on Death. You can pretty much bash the others. Make
sure that you have food and !oFH for the other riders.

The Eyes eliminate the scales. reflection takes care of most other
attacks. None of the insects and the like can really hurt you and
if you like conflict can keep them occupied.

Be sure to gear up your angel. Extra dragon mail and a good weapon can
be useful.

You shouldn't have any problem.

